License rules
-------------

Two rules decide the license of each file:

1. Files inherited from the upstream opencode project are licensed under MIT.
   This includes upstream files that the fork has modified. Their license text
   is `./LICENSE`, with `Copyright (c) 2025 opencode`. Upstream files do not
   carry a separate per-file license header.

2. Every other file written for this fork is licensed under Apache-2.0,
   regardless of when it was written. Their license text is
   `./LICENSE-APACHE`, with `Copyright (c) 2026 LeXwDeX`. Source files written
   for the fork carry these two header lines:

   // SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 LeXwDeX
   // SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

Apache-2.0 section 4 requires redistributors to retain the copyright and
attribution notices from this repository and to include a copy of this NOTICE
file. Modified files must carry prominent notices stating that they were
changed. The attribution statement for the fork-authored code is
`Copyright (c) 2026 LeXwDeX`.

`LICENSE-UPSTREAM.txt` lists every file inherited from upstream opencode that
stays under MIT. Files outside `third_party/`, `patches/`, `LICENSE*` texts,
`bun.lock`, and `*.patch` that are not listed there are Apache-2.0. The
authoritative exclusion rules live in `script/check-license.ts`.

